Package: boot-repair-legacy
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libqt3-mt (>= 3:3.3.7), bash (>= 3.1), util-linux, mount, e2fsprogs, grub, gksu | sudo, cryptsetup
Recommends: dosfstools, lvm2, mdadm, initramfs-tools, rsync
Suggests: kdelibs4c2a
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: CaptainMorgan12 <CaptainMorgan12@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: legacy Boot Bitch recovery GUI and helper (Debian Etch era)
 Legacy Boot Bitch frontend for Debian 4.0 (Etch) and KDE 3.5-era systems:
 the Qt3 GUI (boot-repair-legacy-gui) is the package's entry point and runs
 the ported boot-repair-legacy-helper. The helper keeps the modern Boot
 Bitch command surface and the Repair tool / Repair change status evidence
 contract, but runs on bash 3.1 and pre-systemd userlands. Read-only
 diagnostics are the default; every repair stage stays behind the helper's
 own runtime preflights.
 .
 This package is a separate experimental artifact (version line 0.2.26-etch1);
 it is not the modern Qt6 boot-repair package.
